        <fig id="article-29513.image.f1" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Strabismus Surgery. The medial rectus muscle is being disinserted following pre-placement of polyglactin 910 sutures. A Castroviejo locking forceps grasps the superior pole of the muscle, while a Manson-Aebli scissors does the cutting. A Cook speculum is holding the eyelids. Bticho, <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Desinsertion_du_muscle_CO.jpg">Public Domain</ext-link>, via Wikimedia Commons</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="1280px-Desinsertion_du_muscle_CO" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-29513.s24">
        <fig id="article-29513.image.f2" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Strabismus. Clinical photograph demonstrating ocular misalignment with one eye deviated from the visual axis while the fellow eye maintains fixation. Contributed by S Bhimji, MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="strabismus1" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-29513.s25">
        <fig id="article-29513.image.f3" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Epidemiology of Strabismus. Infographic illustrating the global prevalence, age distribution, sex patterns, familial risk, associated risk factors, and potential consequences of untreated strabismus across different populations. Contributed by K Kaur, MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Screenshot__2026-01-10__at__7.43.28xAM" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-29513.s26">
        <fig id="article-29513.image.f4" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Etiology of Strabismus. Infographic illustrating the major etiologic categories of strabismus, including congenital or developmental, refractive, sensory, neurological, mechanical or restrictive, and systemic or genetic causes, all of which can disrupt ocular alignment and lead to eye misalignment. Contributed by K Kaur, MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Screenshot__2026-01-09__at__8.58.31xPM" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-29513.s27">
        <fig id="article-29513.image.f5" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Etiologic Pathways in Strabismus. Flowchart illustrating how disruption of normal binocular vision due to factors such as abnormal visual input, excessive accommodation, defective neural control, or developmental immaturity leads to failure of sensory or motor fusion and ultimately results in manifest strabismus with either comitant or incomitant deviation. Contributed by MH Kerekes, MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Etiologic__Pathways__in__Strabismus" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-29513.s28">
        <fig id="article-29513.image.f6" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Toxicokinetic Pathway Leading to Acquired Strabismus.&#x000a0;Flowchart illustrating how exposure to drugs, toxins, or metabolic insults progresses through absorption and systemic distribution to affect ocular motor pathways, leading to neuromuscular dysfunction, acquired strabismus with diplopia or gaze limitation, and outcomes ranging from reversible effects to persistent structural damage. Contributed by MH Kerekes, MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Toxicokinetic__Pathway__Leading__to__Acquired__Strabismus" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
